igures — 140,000+ bots [S1] and 500M messages or 500M messages/month (see consistency note below) [S2, S3] — contextualised under a slide heading 'Traction by Apr-16', but these figures are undated as counts and have not been independently verified [C2, C3, C4]. How the company monetises these users, what drives bot creation, and what the expansion strategy is are not found in the extracted evidence.", "after": "Insufficient disclosed data to describe the business model. No revenue model, pricing structure, customer type, or growth mechanism was extracted from the document. The only indicators of commercial activity are the company's self-reported traction figures — 140 000+ bots [S1] and 500M messages with no explicit interval [S2] on page 10, under 'Traction by Apr-16', and separately 500M messages/month [S3] on page 12 (see consistency note below) — but these figures are undated as counts and have not been independently verified [C2, C3, C4]. How the company monetises these users, what drives bot creation, and what the expansion strategy is are not found in the extracted evidence."}, "questions_for_management": {"removed": ["- What is the composition of the $23.1M reported (per Pitch Deck Hunt)ly raised [S4] — how many rounds, at what valuations, and from which investors?"], "added": ["- What is the composition of the $23.1M (per Pitch Deck Hunt) reportedly raised [S4] — how many rounds, at what valuations, and from which investors?"], "rules_added": [], "before": "- Is the 500M messages figure a cumulative total or a monthly rate, and what is the precise measurement date for each traction metric cited in the deck [C2, C3, S2, S3]?\n- What is the current monthly revenue, and what is the primary monetisation mechanism (subscription, usage-based, freemium conversion, or other)?\n- Who are the founders and key team members, and what are their relevant prior roles?\n- What is the current monthly cash burn, and what is the dated cash balance from which runway is calculated?\n- What is the composition of the $23.1M reported (per Pitch Deck Hunt)ly raised [S4] — how many rounds, at what valuations, and from which investors?\n- Is a new fundraising round currently planned or in progress, and if so, what are the intended use of proceeds?\n- What share of the 140,000+ bots [S1] are on paid plans versus free tiers, and what is the average revenue per paying account?\n- What is the customer acquisition cost and the primary channel through which new bots are created on the platform?\n- Who is the target customer — individual developers, small businesses, or enterprises — and what problem does the platform solve for them specifically?\n- What does the competitive landscape look like, and what is ManyChat's stated differentiation from other bot-building or messaging automation platforms?", "after": "- Is the 500M messages figure a cumulative total or a monthly rate, and what is the precise measurement date for each traction metric cited in the deck [C2, C3, S2, S3]?\n- What is the current monthly revenue, and what is the primary monetisation mechanism (subscription, usage-based, freemium conversion, or other)?\n- Who are the founders and key team members, and what are their relevant prior roles?\n- What is the current monthly cash burn, and what is the dated cash balance from which runway is calculated?\n- What is the composition of the $23.1M (per Pitch Deck Hunt) reportedly raised [S4] — how many rounds, at what valuations, and from which investors?\n- Is a new fundraising round currently planned or in progress, and if so, what are the intended use of proceeds?\n- What share of the 140,000+ bots [S1] are on paid plans versus free tiers, and what is the average revenue per paying account?\n- What is the customer acquisition cost and the primary channel through which new bots are created on the platform?\n- Who is the target customer — individual developers, small businesses, or enterprises — and what problem does the platform solve for them specifically?\n- What does the competitive landscape look like, and what is ManyChat's stated differentiation from other bot-building or messaging automation platforms?"}}, "base_replay_equals_stored": {"executive_summary": true, "problem_solution": true, "market_analysis": true, "team_assessment": true, "financial_analysis": true, "risk_assessment": true, "business_model_analysis": true, "information_readiness": true, "supported_points": true, "open_concerns": true, "what_would_change_the_picture": true, "upside_scenario": true, "base_scenario": true, "downside_scenario": true, "zelda_advantage": true, "questions_for_management": true, "evidence_level": true}, "rule_changes_base": {"questions_for_management": ["attribution:Pitch Deck Hunt"]}, "rule_changes_fix": {"business_model_analysis": ["basis_heading_scope"], "questions_for_management": ["attribution:Pitch Deck Hunt"]}, "reversed_items_same_output_and_changes": true, "second_pass_unchanged": true, "every_ref_supplied": true, "refs_in_order_same_as_base_replay": {"executive_summary": true, "problem_solution": true, "market_analysis": true, "team_assessment": true, "financial_analysis": true, "risk_assessment": true, "business_model_analysis": true, "information_readiness": true, "supported_points": true, "open_concerns": true, "what_would_change_the_picture": true, "upside_scenario": true, "base_scenario": true, "downside_scenario": true, "zelda_advantage": true, "questions_for_management": true, "evidence_level": true}}}
